# 🎯 Pentest Learning Dashboard

A professional, production-ready learning management dashboard built for mastering Web Security and Penetration Testing. Designed with a senior engineering mindset for maintainability and extensibility.

## 📊 Features

✅ **Real-time Progress Tracking**
- Phase completion percentage
- Lab mastery tracking (0-100%)
- Learning hours logged
- Consecutive day streaks

✅ **Comprehensive Dashboard Widgets**
- Hero stats (KPIs at a glance)
- Learning progress indicators
- Active labs panel with difficulty badges
- Skills proficiency tracker
- Phase milestones timeline

✅ **Professional Design**
- Security-focused color palette (Indigo, Emerald, Red)
- WCAG AA compliant contrast ratios
- Responsive grid layout (mobile → desktop)
- Semantic color usage (success, warning, danger)

✅ **Developer-Friendly Architecture**
- Centralized design system (no scattered colors/spacing)
- Reusable component library
- Widget-based extensibility (add/remove/reorder)
- TypeScript with strict typing
- Well-documented code patterns

## 🚀 Quick Start

### Installation

```bash
# Copy the files to your React project
cp pentest-dashboard.tsx src/components/dashboard/
cp design-system-colors.ts src/styles/
cp design-system-tokens.ts src/styles/
cp ARCHITECTURE-GUIDE.ts src/docs/

# Install dependencies (if not already installed)
npm install react lucide-react
```

### Basic Usage

```tsx
import PentestDashboard from './components/dashboard/pentest-dashboard';

export default function App() {
  return <PentestDashboard />;
}
```

### Connecting Real Data

Replace mock data with your API:

```tsx
// In PentestDashboard component
const [dashboardData, setDashboardData] = useState<DashboardData | null>(null);

useEffect(() => {
  fetch('/api/dashboard/data')
    .then(r => r.json())
    .then(data => {
      setDashboardData(data);
      // Also fetch labs, skills, milestones
    })
    .catch(err => console.error('Failed to load dashboard data:', err));
}, []);

if (!dashboardData) return <div>Loading...</div>;
return <HeroStats data={dashboardData} />;
```

