## 📦 Widget System

The dashboard uses widgets that can be dynamically added/removed.

### Current Widgets

```tsx
const widgets = [
  'hero-stats',      // KPI cards
  'progress',        // Learning progress
  'labs',            // Active labs
  'skills',          // Skills tracker
  'milestones',      // Phase milestones
];
```

### Adding a Custom Widget

1. **Create the component:**

```tsx
interface MyWidgetData {
  title: string;
  data: string[];
}

const MyCustomWidget: React.FC<{data: MyWidgetData}> = ({data}) => (
  <Card>
    <div style={{...typography.h4, color: colors.text.primary}}>
      {data.title}
    </div>
    <ul>
      {data.data.map(item => (
        <li key={item}>{item}</li>
      ))}
    </ul>
  </Card>
);
```

2. **Add mock data:**

```tsx
const mockMyWidget: MyWidgetData = {
  title: 'My Custom Widget',
  data: ['Item 1', 'Item 2', 'Item 3'],
};
```

3. **Add to renderWidget():**

```tsx
case 'my-widget':
  return <MyCustomWidget key={widgetId} data={mockMyWidget} />;
```

4. **Add to widgets array:**

```tsx
const [widgets, setWidgets] = useState<string[]>([
  'hero-stats',
  'progress',
  'labs',
  'skills',
  'milestones',
  'my-widget',  // ← Add here
]);
```

### Reordering Widgets

```tsx
// Drag and drop implementation (example)
const moveWidget = (fromIndex: number, toIndex: number) => {
  const newWidgets = [...widgets];
  const [movedWidget] = newWidgets.splice(fromIndex, 1);
  newWidgets.splice(toIndex, 0, movedWidget);
  setWidgets(newWidgets);
  
  // Save to localStorage
  localStorage.setItem('dashboardWidgets', JSON.stringify(newWidgets));
};
```

